# tools/t/tablecloth_glow_tend_witness.rish -- Tablecloth's Glow desks, and the drift they cannot
# hide.
#
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/t/tablecloth_glow_tend_witness.rish
#
# WHY THIS RUNG. Every other infrastructure vane carrying a bound worth naming already stood in
# the shape museum when this rung was built -- Aurora four pedestals, Mantra four, Caravan three,
# Tally six, Comlink one, which became two when Comlink's payload ceiling took its own desk on
# 20260830.
# Tablecloth stood there not at all, with zero Glow desks of any kind, while `brushstroke/
# tablecloth.rye` publishes the catalog capacity that the Brix-facing manifest and the four
# `comlink/guest_tablecloth_query_*` wires both lean on. A bound nothing names outside its own
# source is a bound only its author can check. This holds the pedestals and the guard that keeps
# them honest.
#
# THE FOUR PEDESTALS, AND WHY EACH IS A DIFFERENT KIND. `max_artifacts` is a literal
# tablecloth.rye spells for itself, so its desk is compared against that one file.
# `max_content_bytes` is a DERIVATION -- `= beading.max_resin_bytes` -- so tablecloth.rye names the
# bound and mantra/beading.rye decides it. The desk's number is therefore compared against the
# deciding room, and the derivation is read as a fact of its own: respell it as a literal and every
# number still agrees while the link is gone, so the next honest raise of `max_resin_bytes` would
# move one room and leave the other behind with nothing to say so.
#
# The third is neither: `ClothError` is a SET of nine refusal paths, and its desk displays that
# set's SIZE. A count read against a count agrees while the set underneath has changed -- rename
# one path, or drop one and add another, and nine is still nine -- so this desk lists the names and
# the guard compares them as sets. Two readings carry it, and they are the two that can fire apart:
# the desk agrees with ITSELF (the number under `example` equals how many names it lists) and the
# desk agrees with the RYE (its names, sorted, equal ClothError's). Their conjunction gives the
# count agreement for free, so a third reading would be one more copy of the same fact.
#
# THE FOURTH IS A NUMBER WITH AN ALPHABET STANDING BESIDE IT, which is what REDS %354 cost a round
# to learn. `max_name = 48` bounds how LONG an artifact's name may be, and the manifest grammar
# needs something else entirely: that a name carry neither of the two bytes the line is split on.
# Those are different facts, and neither follows from the other -- so the desk shows the number
# AND lists the bytes, and the guard reads three things that can each fail while the other two
# agree. The number equals `max_name`. The bytes listed equal the bytes `name_is_one_field`
# actually refuses -- add a third to the wall and a length-only guard stays perfectly quiet. And
# `store_artifact` still consults that wall, because a function refusing exactly the right bytes
# refuses nothing at all while no caller asks it.
#
# Unlike the error desk, this one's `example` is not a count of its own list, so it cannot
# contradict itself: a length and an alphabet are two facts, and each is read against the Rye
# rather than against its neighbor.
#
# AND EVERY BOUND DESK SPELLS ITS NUMBER TWICE, which pressing this bound is what found. A bound
# pedestal writes its value in the `shape` line and again under `example`, and until 20260830 this
# scan read only the second -- so a hand raising a bound in the Rye and under `example` could leave
# the shape line behind, and every reading stayed quiet because the drift never left the desk.
# Both spellings are read now, for all three bound desks; the error desk is not asked, since its
# number is a set's SIZE and its shape line says so in words rather than naming a bound.
#
# WHAT IS PROVEN, on metal.
#   All four placards read in the order src/shape/PLACARD.md seats: name, shape, invariant,
#   example, readers, nib.
#   The catalog pedestal names the Rye file its number comes from. The content pedestal names BOTH
#   rooms -- the file that declares the bound and the file that holds the number -- because a
#   derived bound owes a reader two addresses.
#   The number each pedestal shows EQUALS the number its source publishes: `max_artifacts` and
#   `max_name` from brushstroke/tablecloth.rye, `max_resin_bytes` from mantra/beading.rye. The scan
#   reads both sides and compares; it carries no value of its own, so raising either bound honestly
#   leaves the guard quiet -- proven as a welcome, not assumed.
#   tablecloth.rye still DERIVES its content budget from beading's resin budget.
#   The error pedestal lists the refusal paths ClothError declares, and the names it lists equal
#   the names the Rye declares -- compared as sorted sets, so a rename cannot pass under a count
#   that has not moved. Its own `example` equals how many names it lists, so the number displayed
#   is a reading of the list rather than a claim standing beside it.
#   The name pedestal lists the bytes `name_is_one_field` refuses, compared as sorted sets, and
#   `store_artifact` still consults that wall -- so the invariant the desk displays stays wired
#   rather than merely written.
#   All four desks lower through Glow, build through the Zig toolchain, and run to EXIT:0.
#   Each bound pedestal agrees with ITSELF: the number in its `shape` line equals the number under
#   `example`, so a bound desk's two spellings cannot part inside one file.
#   Every reading refuses from the other side: forty-two plantings in a throwaway pen, each
#   caught by the reading it was planted against, and six honest trees walking free -- among them a
#   tenth refusal path added in all three rooms at once, and a third reserved byte added to the
#   wall and to its desk together. Those walk free because the SCAN carries no roster of its own:
#   it compares two rooms and holds no value.
#
# WHERE A ROSTER DOES LIVE, said plainly, because the sentence above is true of the scan and not of
# this file. This witness PINS two lists the scan deliberately declines to hold -- the nine
# ClothError names, and the two reserved bytes -- so changing either surface reds here even where
# the scan welcomes it. That is a pin rather than a comparison, and it is deliberate: a module's
# refusal vocabulary and the alphabet its store forbids are both published surfaces, and moving one
# is worth a hand's eye. The cost is one line edited here on an honest change, and the reason is
# written down so the next hand meets a review gate rather than a mystery.
#
# THE CLAIM ABOVE WAS FALSE FOR FOUR READINGS UNTIL 20260905, and how it stayed false is the part
# worth keeping. The four `*_example_missing` verdicts -- one per pedestal -- had no planting, and
# the obvious one does not reach them: deleting a desk's `example` line takes a keyword out of the
# placard, so `placard_wrong` answers one reading earlier and the verdict under it never fires.
# What reaches it is an example the pedestal cannot read as a number, `example    forty-eight`,
# which keeps the placard whole and empties the reading. So the mutation a hand would try proved a
# DIFFERENT reading and looked like coverage. Cases 45 through 48 plant the one that lands.
#
# WHAT IS NOT PROVEN. Whether thirty-two is the right capacity, five hundred twelve the right
# budget, forty-eight the right name length, and nine the right number of ways to refuse -- those
# are Tablecloth's and Mantra's own design questions, and a pedestal only displays what the source
# decided. And any behavior of the store itself, which tools/b/buhr_tablecloth_witness.rish holds
# on real bytes -- including, from 20260830.053148, every one of the nine refusal paths this desk
# names, and the two store refusals the name wall makes.

say "tablecloth-tend: Language EN -- Tablecloth holds a thing by what it is, and it now holds four of its own facts in the shape museum: three bounds, and the whole set of ways it refuses."
say "tablecloth-tend: Style Gauge -- each placard reads in the museum's seated order, and each number it shows is compared to the source rather than remembered."
say "tablecloth-tend: Lens TAME -- bound everything and say why: the catalog names its maximums, the pedestals name the maximums, and this proves each pair is one number."

say "tablecloth-tend: the pedestals against their sources..."
let scan = run ["sh" "tools/fixtures/t/tablecloth_glow_tend_scan.sh"]
assert scan.ok else "tablecloth-tend: a pedestal and its source disagree -- read the verdict line"
say scan.out
assert scan.out contains "verdict=agree" else "tablecloth-tend: each pedestal and its source must name one number"
assert scan.out contains "citation=yes" else "tablecloth-tend: a pedestal names the source its number came from"
assert scan.out contains "content_citation=yes" else "tablecloth-tend: a derived bound's pedestal names both the declaring and the deciding room"
assert scan.out contains "desk_bound=32" else "tablecloth-tend: the catalog desk's shape line and its example are one number"
assert scan.out contains "content_desk_bound=512" else "tablecloth-tend: the content desk's shape line and its example are one number"
assert scan.out contains "name_desk_bound=48" else "tablecloth-tend: the name desk's shape line and its example are one number"
assert scan.out contains "cloth_derives=yes" else "tablecloth-tend: the content budget must still follow beading's resin budget"
assert scan.out contains "placard_order=name shape invariant example readers nib" else "tablecloth-tend: the placard's six lines keep their seated order"
assert scan.out contains "content_placard_order=name shape invariant example readers nib" else "tablecloth-tend: the second placard keeps the same seated order"
assert scan.out contains "error_placard_order=name shape invariant example readers nib" else "tablecloth-tend: the third placard keeps the same seated order"
assert scan.out contains "name_placard_order=name shape invariant example readers nib" else "tablecloth-tend: the fourth placard keeps the same seated order"
assert scan.out contains "error_citation=yes" else "tablecloth-tend: the error pedestal names the Rye file its names come from"
assert scan.out contains "name_citation=yes" else "tablecloth-tend: the name pedestal names the Rye file its number and its wall come from"
assert scan.out contains "wall_wired=yes" else "tablecloth-tend: store_artifact must still consult name_is_one_field, or the desk's invariant is only written"
say "field GREEN -- all four pedestals stand on what their sources publish, each set compared as a set"

say "tablecloth-tend: the two pinned rosters -- a review gate, not a comparison (see the header)..."
assert scan.out contains "error_desk_names=BadManifest CatalogFull ContentTooLarge NameEmpty NameHasSeparator NameTaken NameTooLong Overflow UnknownArtifact" else "tablecloth-tend: the nine ClothError names are PINNED here; if the set changed on purpose, move this line and its twin"
assert scan.out contains "rye_error_names=BadManifest CatalogFull ContentTooLarge NameEmpty NameHasSeparator NameTaken NameTooLong Overflow UnknownArtifact" else "tablecloth-tend: the Rye's own refusal set is pinned beside the desk's, so both move together or neither does"
assert scan.out contains "name_desk_bytes=newline space" else "tablecloth-tend: the two reserved bytes are PINNED here; widening the wall is a review gate, so move this line and its twin"
assert scan.out contains "rye_wall_bytes=newline space" else "tablecloth-tend: the wall's own bytes are pinned beside the desk's, so both move together or neither does"
say "pins GREEN -- the refusal vocabulary and the forbidden alphabet stand where they stood"

say "tablecloth-tend: the control, both ways..."
let control = run ["sh" "tools/fixtures/t/tablecloth_glow_tend_control.sh"]
assert control.ok else "tablecloth-tend: the control must complete"
say control.out
assert control.out contains "welcomes=6" else "tablecloth-tend: an honest tree, three honest raises, an honestly added refusal path, and an honestly widened wall must all walk free"
assert control.out contains "refusals=42" else "tablecloth-tend: every reading must refuse from its own side"
assert control.out contains "wrong=0" else "tablecloth-tend: no case may land on the side it was not planted for"
assert control.out contains "control_verdict=ok" else "tablecloth-tend: the control must agree with itself"
say "RED and GREEN paths proven -- forty-two plantings refused, six honest trees welcomed"

let zig = "vendor/zig-toolchain/zig"
let desk = "src/shape/shape-tablecloth-catalog-capacity.glow"
let content_desk = "src/shape/shape-tablecloth-content-budget.glow"
let error_desk = "src/shape/shape-tablecloth-error-paths.glow"
let name_desk = "src/shape/shape-tablecloth-name-bound.glow"

say "tablecloth-tend: lower, build, run the catalog pedestal..."
let gate = run ["env" "RYE_ZIG=${zig}" "sh" "tools/g/glow_run_worker.sh" desk]
assert gate.ok else "tablecloth-tend: the catalog pedestal must lower, build, and run"
assert gate.out contains "EXIT:0" else "tablecloth-tend: the catalog pedestal did not exit 0"

say "tablecloth-tend: lower, build, run the content pedestal..."
let gate2 = run ["env" "RYE_ZIG=${zig}" "sh" "tools/g/glow_run_worker.sh" content_desk]
assert gate2.ok else "tablecloth-tend: the content pedestal must lower, build, and run"
assert gate2.out contains "EXIT:0" else "tablecloth-tend: the content pedestal did not exit 0"

say "tablecloth-tend: lower, build, run the error-paths pedestal..."
let gate3 = run ["env" "RYE_ZIG=${zig}" "sh" "tools/g/glow_run_worker.sh" error_desk]
assert gate3.ok else "tablecloth-tend: the error-paths pedestal must lower, build, and run"
assert gate3.out contains "EXIT:0" else "tablecloth-tend: the error-paths pedestal did not exit 0"

say "tablecloth-tend: lower, build, run the name-bound pedestal..."
let gate4 = run ["env" "RYE_ZIG=${zig}" "sh" "tools/g/glow_run_worker.sh" name_desk]
assert gate4.ok else "tablecloth-tend: the name-bound pedestal must lower, build, and run"
assert gate4.out contains "EXIT:0" else "tablecloth-tend: the name-bound pedestal did not exit 0"
say "metal GREEN -- all four desks lower through Glow, build through Zig, and run"

say "GREEN: tablecloth Glow Tend -- max_artifacts, max_content_bytes, max_name with the alphabet its wall removes, and the nine ClothError paths stand on pedestals, each compared to the room that decides it rather than copied from it."
